'Skip to content\nFamily Threads\n\nWhat is a number?\n\n1\nWhat is a game?\n2\nWhat is a tool?\n3\nWhat is a language?\n4\nWhat is a number?\nwhole numbers\nfractions\nnegative numbers\nzero\nbus numbers\n\u03c0 (pi)\n\nMake the strongest claim that is true of these numbers. Then look.\n\n\u2026 of these numbers can be added together.\n\nAll\nMost\nSome\nNone\nLook\nAbout Family Threads\nHow to play\nSix cards show things we call by one name: games, tools, languages or numbers. Make the strongest claim that is true of them: all, most, some or none.\nThread every card into one chain, each link a feature two neighbours share.\nA newcomer arrives. Link it with \u201cboth\u201d, or keep it at the edge with \u201cunlike\u201d.\n\nEnglish you practise: all / most / some / none of these; both \u2026 and; unlike.'
              </p>
