@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+FAIL — revise the answer model and teaching copy before release. No blocker found; 5 major and 3 minor findings.
+
+Tested 2026-11-01 against the existing production server at `http://localhost:3418`, using Python Playwright Chromium: 390×844 touch phone and 1280×860 desktop, fresh storage. Reached all three sessions through **Sessions** and completed all 12 rounds on each device. Tried wrong answers, hints/explanations, and mid-round reloads. Saved placements, examples, chains, and selections survived. No captured JavaScript/console errors; desktop captured no failed requests. Server and `src/`, `public/`, `e2e/` were untouched.
+
+**Findings**
+
+1. **Major — zero is wrongly denied a measurement use.** `src/games/family/rounds.ts:111`: linking whole numbers → zero with “can measure an amount” is rejected. As a learner, I can defend “zero litres.” **Fix:** add `measure` to zero's features. [Phone evidence](../qa/playtest-3/phone-family-zero-measure-rejected.png).
+
+2. **Major — number values and their uses are graded as if interchangeable.** `src/games/family/rounds.ts:98`, `:108`, `:112`, `:211`: “All … can be added together” rejects bus numbers, although 42 + 7 is valid arithmetic; the shirt round says whole numbers cannot name things, although shirt 7 does exactly that. **Fix:** label cards as uses (“counting apples”, “identifying a bus route”) and ask about what the numbers **do here**, replacing the bus hint with “Adding route labels does not tell you how many buses there are.” [Addition rejection](../qa/playtest-3/phone-family-1-all-wrong.png), [naming rejection](../qa/playtest-3/phone-family-whole-name-rejected.png).
+
+3. **Major — the accepted -ing explanation omits its own exceptions.** `src/games/pupil/levels.ts:303` says to double a final consonant after a single vowel in a stressed syllable, without excluding w/x/y. Yet `engine.ts:158` excludes them, and the displayed test accepts **playing**. **Fix:** add “Do not double w, x or y” to the explanation and summary at `levels.ts:278`. [Displayed rule and test](../qa/playtest-3/phone-pupil-8-explain-wrong.png); [spelling reference](https://sites.google.com/education.vic.gov.au/phonograms/stage-4/rule-9).
+
+4. **Major — §67 is presented as a history it does not give.** `src/content/sources.ts:162` claims fractions earned their name through measuring, negatives through addition, and bus numbers connect only through digits. Anscombe's §67 proposes overlapping relationships, not those historical causes or that exclusive connection. **Fix:** describe these as this game's comparisons: “Fractions and whole numbers can measure amounts; negative and whole numbers can be added; route numbers identify buses.” [Rendered gloss](../qa/playtest-3/phone-family-source.png); [Anscombe §67](https://manuals.plus/m/d1732a8b85530469e1e27b7031baaab81c11e9452f00cc5c6b7a8207fd81d4bc.pdf#page=20).
+
+5. **Major — the pupil's twist explanations overclaim their citations.** `src/games/pupil/levels.ts:271` uses §217 to explain acquisition of irregular forms; that passage concerns justification for following rules. At `:312`, §§198–201 do not make hearing a prerequisite for spelling. **Fix:** teach “have → has; be → is” and “keep -ee: see → seeing; drop silent e: make → making”; separately label the practice analogy. Use word-only `see → seing`, avoiding the awkward context-free “I am seeing it.” [p-7 feedback](../qa/playtest-3/phone-pupil-7-wrong-twist.png), [p-8 feedback](../qa/playtest-3/phone-pupil-8-wrong-twist.png); [Anscombe §§198–201](https://manuals.plus/m/d1732a8b85530469e1e27b7031baaab81c11e9452f00cc5c6b7a8207fd81d4bc.pdf#page=44), [§217](https://manuals.plus/m/d1732a8b85530469e1e27b7031baaab81c11e9452f00cc5c6b7a8207fd81d4bc.pdf#page=46).
+
+6. **Minor — inaccurate quotation.** `src/content/sources.ts:160` drops **it** from Anscombe's “give it an indirect relationship.” **Fix:** restore **it**. [§67 original](https://manuals.plus/m/d1732a8b85530469e1e27b7031baaab81c11e9452f00cc5c6b7a8207fd81d4bc.pdf#page=20).
+
+7. **Minor — the last negation hint contradicts accepted solutions.** `src/games/scene/rounds.ts:273` says “only one place is left”; the ball **on the box** also passes all three clauses, in addition to the free shelf place beside the book. **Fix:** remove the uniqueness claim or explicitly name the shelf position as one solution. [Hint](../qa/playtest-3/phone-scene-6-hint.png), [accepted alternative](../qa/playtest-3/phone-scene-6-on-box-right.png).
+
+8. **Minor — obsolete rejection survives an edited answer and reload.** `src/games/family/FamilyGame.tsx:441`: reject shirt + whole numbers + naming, change whole numbers to bus numbers, then reload. The correct current sentence retains the previous rejection until submitted again. **Fix:** clear `result` when the mode, comparison card, or feature changes. [Phone](../qa/playtest-3/phone-family-newcomer-reload.png), [desktop](../qa/playtest-3/desktop-family-4-reload.png).
+
+**Evidence and limits**
+
+Commands: `python qa/playtest-3/phone.py` (scene), plus `pupil` and `family`; `python qa/playtest-3/desktop-scene.py`; `python qa/playtest-3/desktop-family-pupil.py`. These are interaction records, not assertions that the teaching is correct. Screenshots and JSON transcripts are in `qa/playtest-3/`; the phone `*-done.png` and desktop `*-end.png` captures show completion.
+
+All seven requested family WebPs were inspected directly and in the rendered cards: no clear picture/text contradiction found. The thermometer is below zero; the basket is empty; bus 42 and shirt 7 are legible. TLP 4.0621 matches [Ogden](https://www.wittgensteinproject.org/w/index.php/Tractatus_Logico-Philosophicus_(English)#4.0621); Go On's §185 and §198 quotations match Anscombe apart from typography and marked omission. The supplied Jackson wiki references had nothing relevant to this task ([index](C:/Users/Administrator/Documents/projects/LLMwiki/index.md)).
+
+**Also done:** retained replay scripts and browser-error evidence to make the findings reproducible. Undo: remove this report and this task's `qa/playtest-3/` artifacts; no application changes to revert.
+
+**Not covered:** physical phones, WebKit/Firefox, assistive technology, every possible placement/comparison, and other sessions. This was a B1 reading simulation, not observation of recruited learners. No build, unit-test, or full accessibility suite was run, and no fixes were applied.
